  "worked_solution": "The area of the lateral surface area of the cone is given by\n\n$$\nA=A(r)=\\pi r\u2113,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the base of the cone and $\u2113$ is its slant height.\n\nWe are given that $\u2113=2r,$ so we can express the area $A$ as a function of the radius $r$ by substituting $\u2113=2r$ into the formula above. We get\n\n$$\nA=\\pi r(2r)=2\\pi {r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(r)$ with respect to its radius $r$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{\u2032}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(2\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\pi (2r) \\\\  & =4\\pi r.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
